        "question": "A 68-year-old man with a 50 pack-year smoking history presents with haemoptysis and weight loss. CT chest shows a 5 cm central mass in the right hilum with extensive mediastinal lymphadenopathy. Bronchoscopy and biopsy confirm small cell lung cancer (SCLC). Which statement about SCLC compared to non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) is MOST accurate?",
